    "title": "🧪 Final exam — 40.0%|||🧪 Final exam — 40.0%",
    "slug": "ecr301-flm-thi-4",
    "type": "DOCUMENT",
    "description": "Final exam 40.0%",
    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ECR301 · Assessment 4/4</span>\n<h2>Final exam</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14238 · assessment table (verbatim)</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">ECR301 · Đầu điểm 4/4</span>\n<h2>Final exam</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14238 · bảng đánh giá (nguyên văn)</p></div>\n<div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type / Loại</span><span class=\"v\">Final exam</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Weight / Trọng số</span><span class=\"v\">40.0%</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Parts / Số phần</span><span class=\"v\">2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Completion criteria / Điều kiện hoàn thành</span><span class=\"v\">4</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Duration / Thời lượng</span><span class=\"v\">90'</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">CLO</span><span class=\"v\">All LOs</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Question type / Dạng câu hỏi</span><span class=\"v\">1. Students will be given a new, short non-fiction article (e.g., an op-ed, a short report, or an excerpt from a book) on a topic related to the course themes (e.g., technology, social issues, leadership). They will have to perform a detailed critical analysis of this text.2. Short Writing Task Write a short response (250 words)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">No. of questions / Số câu</span><span class=\"v\">Part 1: The Critical Reading AnalysisPart 2: Writing task in response to the reading in the critical reading analysis</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Knowledge &amp; skill / Kiến thức &amp; kỹ năng</span><span class=\"v\">Knowledge and skills in studied chapter(s)</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Grading guide / Hướng dẫn chấm</span><span class=\"v\">in exam room, using computer or papers</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Note / Ghi chú</span><span class=\"v\">Part 1. (70%)<br><br>Instructions:<br><br>- Thesis and Purpose: Identify the author's main thesis or purpose. What is the author trying to convince the reader of?<br><br>- Evidence Evaluation: Identify distinct pieces of evidence or reasoning the author uses. For each one, evaluate its strength and identify its type (e.g., anecdote, statistic, quotation, appeal to emotion).<br><br>- Assumptions and Bias: Identify underlying assumptions the author holds. How might these assumptions influence the author's argument?<br><br>- Counter-Argument: Briefly outline a potential counter-argument to the author's central thesis. What evidence would a critical reader need to find to support this opposing view?<br><br>Part 2. (30%)<br><br>Instruction:<br><br>Write a short response (~250 words) that addresses the following prompt:<br><br>Prompt:<br><br>&quot;Based on your critical analysis of the provided text, what is your final judgment on the author's argument? Is it a credible, well-supported claim, or is it a flawed and unconvincing one? Your response should not just state your opinion but must explicitly reference at least two specific points from your analysis in Part 1 to justify your conclusion. You must mention at least one strength and one weakness you identified in the author's argument.&quot;</span></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">🧪 Practice papers: <a href=\"/exam?course=ECR301\">Exam Room — ECR301</a> (1 papers: PE).</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">🧪 Đề luyện: <a href=\"/exam?course=ECR301\">Phòng thi — ECR301</a> (1 đề: PE).</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Exam-strategy notes and worked past papers: coming later.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Chiến lược làm bài và chữa đề: sẽ bổ sung sau.</div></div>"
